From 628c0dd1f75febf2c9c690feabfbeeb43900ad3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 09:15:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Revolution skipped leader develop-triggers; Ocean Liner
 charged a phantom CA (553 -> 582)

Two fixes from the Take + Upgrade buckets.

1. `apply.rs::h_revolution` inlined only Isaac Newton trigger and never called
   the shared `on_develop()` helper, so Leonardo da Vinci +1 resource and
   Albert Einstein +3 culture silently never fired on a violent Revolution.
   docs/RULES_SPEC.md line 232 is explicit that a revolution counts as
   developing a technology. Game 7522665: the missing resource in round 11
   starved an Upgrade seven rounds later. The bot suffers from this too.

2. `replay_common.rs` `apply_one()` IncreasePopulation dispatch chose
   `Move::Pop` whenever it was merely LEGAL, ignoring BGO own explicit
   "Ocean Liner Service used" text -- billing a civil action for what is a
   free wonder-granted population increase. Cleared 28 games on its own,
   because the ambiguity recurs across the corpus. Replayer-side.

Full 1011-game sweep: ZERO regressions against BOTH the frozen 509 baseline
and the current 553 base. 29 wins. 582 completed, 532 exact.

Still open, per the notes: a WonderInProgress same-instant journal-ordering
issue in ~3 Take games, plus several Upgrade shortfalls with file/function
pointers.
