From f7f121f1b99e84937f1f6f98ad8c6a00bfb63517 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:11:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] PlayAction: IA same-turn play, Frugality, Robespierre
 Breakthrough, Bach (582 -> 609 complete)

Four engine rule bugs, all found by replaying real BGO human games:
- Cards taken via International Agreement were wrongly marked taken_this_turn
  and blocked from being played the same turn (CoL p.12 / RULES_SPEC line 383).
- Frugality + Trade Routes Agreement: population partly paid by a
  resource-as-food conversion glued onto one journal line with no preceding
  move; mirrors the synthesis the ordinary Pop path already does.
- Robespierre could not fund a Breakthrough revolution with military actions,
  though RB p.15 frames Breakthrough as funding the revolution (CoL p.12).
- J. S. Bach cross-kind theater upgrade could not be funded by a yellow action
  card discount, and Move::BachTheater was unreachable from
  apply_free_civil_move dispatch (RB p.24).

609/1011 complete, 557 exact. Zero regressions against the 582 baseline.
NOTE: unit tests still owed for all four; corpus-verified only.
